  "id": "filtered-speech",
  "term": "filtered speech",
  "definition": "Filtered speech is speech that has been acoustically altered by applying filtering, such as temporal filtering, so that some speech cues are degraded. In research and assessment contexts, it is used to test how well people recognize speech when the signal is less clear, often alongside noise or other listening challenges.",
